## 6. INTELLIGENT VIDEO CLIP DISCOVERY

This is one of the application's most important modules.

The system must identify genuinely useful short-form segments rather than simply selecting random portions of a video.

Evaluate candidate clips according to:

- Strength of the opening.
- Clarity of the central idea.
- Relevance to the target audience.
- Completeness of the argument.
- Practical usefulness.
- Storytelling quality.
- Emotional resonance, when appropriate.
- Potential for audience engagement.
- Independence from surrounding context.
- Suitability for the intended platform.

These scores are editorial estimates, not predictions of guaranteed views or virality.

### Clip requirements

Allow configurable target durations, with sensible defaults between 30 and 60 seconds.

A clip may be shorter or longer when the user explicitly allows it and the content justifies the choice.

For each candidate, return structured data containing:

- Clip ID.
- Proposed title.
- Hook.
- Start timestamp.
- End timestamp.
- Duration.
- Exact opening transcript text.
- Exact closing transcript text.
- Complete transcript for the selected interval.
- Central idea.
- Reason for selection.
- Target audience.
- Recommended platform.
- Suggested caption.
- Suggested on-screen title.
- Call to action.
- Editorial quality score.
- Timing confidence.
- Relevant source segment IDs.
- Validation status.

Use valid JSON that conforms to an application-defined schema.

### Clip boundary validation

The AI must select boundaries using the timestamped transcript.

The application must then:

1. Confirm that the start and end timestamps are valid.
2. Confirm that the timestamps fall within the source media duration.
3. Confirm that the end is later than the start.
4. Calculate the duration programmatically.
5. Check that the selected transcript segments correspond to the intended interval.
6. Identify boundaries that cut through sentences.
7. Flag clips that lack sufficient context.
8. Allow the user to adjust both boundaries.
9. Preview the selected interval before final rendering.

Do not silently adjust a timestamp if doing so changes the meaning of the clip.

When the available transcript does not support precise boundary validation, mark the clip as needing review.

### Clip ranking

Rank candidates using configurable editorial weights.

Provide separate assessments for:

- Opening strength.
- Content clarity.
- Completeness.
- Audience relevance.
- Standalone usefulness.
- Production suitability.

Explain the rationale behind the ranking.

Do not claim that a high score guarantees viral performance.

### Avoid repetitive clips

Check for overlapping or substantially similar candidate segments.

Flag candidates that repeat the same point.

Offer a diverse final selection rather than eight clips with nearly identical messages.

