## 13. SECURITY AND PRIVACY

Implement the following safeguards:

- Keep API keys on the server.
- Validate uploaded files.
- Restrict file operations to approved project directories.
- Avoid shell command injection when invoking FFmpeg.
- Escape and validate user-provided filenames.
- Limit processing concurrency.
- Apply sensible file-size and duration limits.
- Avoid exposing private filesystem paths.
- Do not expose credentials in logs or error messages.
- Clean up temporary files when appropriate.
- Provide a way to delete project data.
- Document where source files and generated assets are stored.
- Do not send source material to third-party services without making the processing behaviour clear.
- Do not use client content to train a model unless the user has explicitly authorised that behaviour.

If multi-user authentication is introduced, implement proper project-level access controls.

Do not represent local-only prototype storage as secure multi-tenant cloud storage.

