## 18. DEFINITION OF DONE

The application is not complete merely because the dashboard looks polished.

A successful implementation must demonstrate the following workflow:

1. The user creates a brand profile.
2. The user creates a project.
3. The user uploads a supported video or timestamped transcript.
4. The application processes the source or explains why processing cannot continue.
5. The AI produces a structured analysis.
6. The application generates a blog, newsletter, and multiple distinct LinkedIn posts.
7. The application identifies short-form video candidates.
8. The user reviews and edits the proposed timestamps.
9. The video engine renders at least one actual clip from the original media.
10. The application produces synchronised captions using available timing information.
11. The user approves the assets.
12. The user downloads a ZIP containing the generated deliverables.
13. The application preserves completed work if an individual stage fails.

All essential functionality must use real application logic.

Do not use hard-coded sample results to simulate completed processing.

If an external integration is unavailable, clearly identify it as unconfigured rather than presenting a mock result as genuine output.

